{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Natural World"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Visiting The Seals "}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "  Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le12ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Writing a Descriptive Paragraph Using the Passive Form "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Verbs may be active or passive. In sentences with active verbs, the subject performs (\"does\") the action. In sentences with passive verbs, the subject receives the action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Passive verbs always have at least two parts: a form of BE and a past participle."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the passive form if you think that the thing receiving the action is more important or should be emphasized. You can also use the passive form if you do not know who is doing the action or if you do not want to say who is doing the action."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The tour was organized by the group leader. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The Seal Conservation society was created by individuals who wanted to protect animals."}, {"type": "example", "content": " In 1997, two-thirds of them were wiped out by a virus."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Many seals were hunted for their meat by poor communities."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Writing About Feelings and Impressions "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You talk about feelings and reactions using adjectives.<br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> are used  to describe how a person feels, like  <span class=\"italic\">annoyed</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">fascinated</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">entertained</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> surprised</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">worried</span> or <span class=\"italic\"> tired</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ing</span> are used to describe things and situations,  like <span class=\"italic\">annoying</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> entertaining</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> surprising</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> worrying </span>or <span class=\"italic\"> tiring. </span>  These adjectives describe the effect something has on a person."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I'm amazed by their speed in the water."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's upsetting and worrying to hear."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's frightening!"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "exhibit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an object or a collection of objects that have been put out in a public space for people to look at"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Welcome to the seal exhibit!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you write about animal conservation."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "endangered"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to describe a type of animal or plant that has become very rare and that could die out completely"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They should be more interested in looking after endangered wildlife."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "virus"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an extremely small living thing that causes a disease and that spreads from one person or animal to another "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These two animals were stuck down with a virus."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conservationist"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who works to protect animals, plants, and natural resources "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Since then, conservationists have worked to increase their numbers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " to strive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to try very hard to do or achieve something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They strive to offer educational materials for schools too."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "longevity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "long life;  the fact of living for many years "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Conservation is essential to the longevity of many species."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "diverse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " different from each other "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our diverse environment could be lost."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob08aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ecosystem"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "everything that exists in a particular environment                   "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: There are many plants and animals in each ecosystem."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob08aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and research an endangered animal from around the world."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write notes including the population left in the wild, conservation efforts and location of animals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write two 60-word paragraphs about what you learned."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use adjectives ending in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> and <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> like <span class=\"italic\">It was interesting to learn about</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the passive voice i.e. <span class=\"italic\">The Monk Seal was almost hunted to extinction by fishermen</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your paragraph(s) aloud to a partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research endangered animals online."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a paragraph about an endangered animal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write the in the passive voice in a paragraph."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write a short descriptive paragraph about nature and the animal world."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write about feelings and impressions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss how to deal with problems."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What is your point of view regarding animal conservation? Are you worried about endangered species? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Would you consider volunteering for an animal rights group?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"