{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn7le12ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn7le12ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Presenter</span>: Welcome to the seal exhibit! These Monk seals were brought here by the Seal Conservation Society.  <br/><span class=\"strong\">Jeffrey</span>: I'm amazed by their speed in the water. Aren't seals common in the wild?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Presenter</span>: There is conflicting information about whether seals are endangered or not. However, it is well documented that the Mediterranean Monk Seal, a species along the coastline of Africa, is critically endangered.  There are only 600 of them remaining in the wild.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jeffrey</span>: That's upsetting and worrying to hear. Only 600?", "id": 1, "image": "engenn7le12ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "33000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Presenter</span>:  In 1997, two-thirds of them were wiped out by a virus. Since then, conservationists have worked to increase their numbers. Many seals were hunted for their meat by poor communities.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Jeffrey</span>: I'm shocked at those numbers. So if conservationists had not decided to try to make a difference, these seals would be extinct? That's frightening!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Presenter</span>: It's very possible. The Seal Conservation society has been in place since 1996.  This non-profit organization has worked to create marine areas to provide food supplies for the seals and the people who live in the area. That way, the Monk seal is not the main food supply in the area.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn7le12ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "78500", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Melissa</span>: Are there they involved with the other animal rights groups?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Presenter</span>:  Yes, they work very closely with other animal rights groups. They also contact political figures to push for further protection of seals and strive to offer educational materials for schools too.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Melissa</span>: If younger generations learn to be compassionate towards animals they should be more interested in looking after endangered wildlife.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Presenter</span>: Exactly! Conservation is essential to the longevity of many species.  If future generations are not committed to protecting endangered animals, our diverse ecosystems could be lost.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le12ob08re2img02.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le12ob08re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn7le12ob08re3vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 2}], "id": 0}]}